From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_oob: drop a frame whose tag cannot be added

skb_ext_add() allocates with GFP_ATOMIC and returns NULL when that
fails, and oob_tag_xmit() then writes the port through the NULL
pointer. Return NULL instead, so the core drops the frame.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_oob.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_oob.c
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@ static struct sk_buff *oob_tag_xmit(stru
 	struct dsa_oob_tag_info *tag_info = skb_ext_add(skb, SKB_EXT_DSA_OOB);
 	struct dsa_port *dp = dsa_user_to_port(dev);
 
+	if (!tag_info)
+		return NULL;
+
 	tag_info->port = dp->index;
 
 	return skb;
